File Management System:
--> comes under java.io.*;

to create a new file:
File = new File("stu.txt");
//here .txt extention is maditory.

1. Methods & Method	Purpose of File Class
//import java.io.File;

createNewFile()	Creates a new file
exists()	Checks if file exists
getName()	Returns file name
getPath()	Returns file path
getAbsolutePath()	Returns full path
canRead()	Checks if file is readable
canWrite()	Checks if file is writable
length()	Returns file size
delete()	Deletes file
mkdir()	Creates a folder
mkdirs()	Creates nested folders
isFile()	Checks if it is a file
isDirectory()	Checks if it is a directory
list()	Lists files in folder
renameTo()	Renames file
lastModified()	Returns last modified time
setReadOnly()	Makes file read-only
rename() Reanames the existing file 
flush() Remove the bufferspace

Example Using File Methods
import java.io.File;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        File file = new File("student.txt");

        System.out.println(file.exists());
        System.out.println(file.getName());
        System.out.println(file.getPath());
        System.out.println(file.canRead());
        System.out.println(file.canWrite());
    }
}

2. Methods & Method	Purpose of FileWriter
//import java.io.FileWriter;

write()	Writes data into file
append()	Adds data at end
close()	Closes file

Example
FileWriter fw = new FileWriter("data.txt");

fw.write("Hello");
fw.append(" World");

fw.close();

3. Methods & Method Purpose of FileReader
read()	Reads character
close()	Closes reader

4. Methods & Method	Purpose of BufferedReader
readLine()	Reads one line
close()	Closes reader

5. Methods & Method	Purpose of BufferedWriter
write()	Writes data
newLine()	Adds new line
close()	Closes writer

6. Methods & Method	Purpose of Scanner
hasNextLine()	Checks next line exists
nextLine()	Reads line
close()	Closes scanner


--> whenever we open the filewriter, we have to close it without fail.
--> To append data, use:
    FileWriter("filename", true)
    here true means append mode.
--> Without append mode it will remove old content and write new content only.




